 | `ROSEMARY_SHADER_CACHE` | `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/rosemary/metal-shaders` | Where Metal shaders translated to SPIR-V are cached, together with each GPU's Vulkan pipeline cache (`pipelines-<vendor>-<device>-<uuid>.bin`), so a second run neither retranslates shaders nor recompiles pipelines. Falls back to `$HOME/.cache/rosemary/metal-shaders`. Each build of the translator keeps its own subdirectory and removes the others; `ROSEMARY_SHADER_CACHE_KEEP` keeps them. Set to `off`, `0` or the empty string to disable both caches. |
 | `ROSEMARY_SCREEN_REFRESH_RATE` | unset | Hertz that guests are told the display refreshes at, in place of the host's mode: `NSScreen`/`UIScreen` `maximumFramesPerSecond` and the refresh-interval properties. |
 | `ROSEMARY_EXPOSE_LIBSYSTEM_EXTENSIONS` | unset | Whether to enable Rosemary specific extensions useful for implementing out of tree features to Rosemary. Disabled by default for full environment accuracy. Set to `1` to enable it - See `crates/darwin/src/rosemary/mod.rs` for more details. |
+| `ROSEMARY_VIDEO_DECODERS` | `vulkan,vaapi,cuda` (`vulkan,vaapi,cuda,gstreamer` in a build with the `videotoolbox` crate's `gstreamer` feature) | The H.264 decoders VideoToolbox decompression sessions may use, in the order they are tried. `vulkan`, `vaapi` and `cuda` are FFmpeg 8 (`libavcodec.so.62` and `libavutil.so.60`, loaded when first needed, never linked) over that hardware API; each is tried once per process on a tiny clip before it is used, and skipped if the host's FFmpeg, driver or GPU cannot decode it. VA-API tries each render node under `/dev/dri/by-path`, and Vulkan FFmpeg's default device and then each device by index. FFmpeg's software fallback is never used by these. `gstreamer` is GStreamer's software `avdec_h264`, only in a build with that feature, which links GStreamer. A decoder specification asking for hardware (`RequireHardwareAcceleratedVideoDecoder`) passes over `gstreamer`, and one that disables it (`EnableHardwareAcceleratedVideoDecoder` false) passes over the rest. `none` turns decoding off. With no decoder that works, sessions report `kVTCouldNotFindVideoDecoderErr` and the program falls back to its own decoding. A session announces the decoder it got, and why there is none, on stderr, and says when its first frame reaches the program. |
 
